Feature: slice-3 / accept-invite-page
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-3
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §9 (Invitation flow end-to-end)

What was built
==============
- src/lib/register/schema.ts — acceptInviteSchema covers email +
  password + name + modality + ui-language + ToS.
- src/components/register/AcceptInviteForm.tsx — client form. Submit:
    1. auth.signUpWithEmail → Firebase + sendEmailVerification.
    2. identityClient.acceptInvitation({token, firebaseUid, ...}).
    3. window.location → verify-email interstitial.
  Connect error code mapping for invitation issues:
    - Code.NotFound       → "invalid token"
    - Code.PermissionDenied (msg has "expired") → "expired"
    - Code.PermissionDenied (default)           → "already accepted"
- src/app/[locale]/accept-invite/page.tsx — server shell. Reads
  `?token=` from search params. If missing, renders the magma-bordered
  "missing token" alert instead of the form.

The page is intentionally hosted on the marketing origin as a stopgap
until Slice 5 brings up the Flutter Web shell at app.superwizor.ai.
notification-svc's email-template URL is the single switch between
origins.

Email-not-in-link gap (documented)
==================================
docs/18 §9 email link is `…/accept-invite?token=<base64url>`. The
proto exposes no GetInvitationByToken RPC, so the page asks the
invitee to retype their email. The backend's AcceptInvitation
handler cross-checks the SHA-256 of the incoming token against
invitations.token_hash AND verifies the row's email matches —
mismatch surfaces as Code.NotFound / PermissionDenied which the
component maps to user-friendly copy. Two future paths:
  A) Extend the link to `?token=X&email=Y` (notification-svc tweak).
  B) Add a GetInvitationByToken RPC for one-shot pre-flight lookup.

